<GuideLayout
  title="Supply Chain Resilience Strategy for Activewear Brands"
  type="SUPPLY CHAIN"
  description="How activewear brands can build supply chain resilience through supplier vetting, fabric planning, backup options, reorder systems and production visibility."
>
  <p>Activewear brands face demand swings, fabric delays, shipping pressure and seasonal launch deadlines. A resilient supply chain does not mean buying from many random suppliers. It means building a controlled system with visibility and backup planning.</p>

  <h2>Core Resilience Levers</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Confirm factory capacity before peak season.</li>
    <li>Approve core fabrics early and keep alternatives ready.</li>
    <li>Use repeatable fits for best-selling styles.</li>
    <li>Plan reorder windows instead of waiting until stock is gone.</li>
    <li>Keep communication records for sampling and production changes.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Ready Stock Plus Custom Development</h2>
  <p>Many brands use ready-to-ship private label styles for speed while developing custom OEM products for differentiation. This hybrid system reduces launch risk and protects long-term uniqueness.</p>

  <h2>Fitclo Support</h2>
  <p>Fitclo helps brands coordinate fabric selection, sampling, capacity planning, production control and shipping so sourcing decisions are easier to repeat.</p>
</GuideLayout>
